# Response headers for everything Cloudflare serves from dist/.
#
# This file is the deployed counterpart of what internal/api sets in Go. The
# two have to agree, because /api/v1/events.json is served from here in
# production and from `htxdev serve` locally, and a client that works against
# one should work against the other.
#
# Not applied to anything generated by Worker code, only to static assets.
# There is no Worker script here, so that caveat does not bite yet.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# The API. Wide open on purpose, and for the reason internal/api/middleware.go
# gives: one public GET of public event listings, no cookies, no credentials,
# no state. Access-Control-Allow-Credentials is deliberately absent, which is
# what keeps "*" safe. The moment anything here is authenticated, this has to
# become an allowlist.
/api/*
  Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, HEAD, OPTIONS
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=600

# Astro fingerprints these filenames, so a change produces a new URL and an old
# URL is never stale. Immutable tells a browser it need not revalidate at all.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
